  "description": "Working principle：Every 30 seconds, these mole repeller spikes emit ultra-low frequency sonic pulses penetrate the soil. Thesound is extremely irritating to moles because they are virtually blind and thus overly sensitive tosound and vibrations. The sonic pulses encourage underground varmints to vacate the property and alsodiscourage return visits.Easy installation in three steps:1.Make a pilot hole in the ground using a wooden rod or steel rod.2.Insert the mole spike into the ground, make sure the top is above the surface roughly 1 or 2 inches. Placesoil around the unit, securing.3.Turn on the switch and expose yourself to the sun for 24 hours.Extensive coverage:Operates in a circular pattern, approximately 40 ft. in diameter. So it is recommended to use 12 solarmole repeller units per acre, insert them every 60 inch.NOTE:Although the solar mole repellent is waterproof, it cannot be immersed in water for a long time, which willaffect its service life. When encountering heavy rain or rainstorm weather, please take it out of the groundfirst, wait for the accumulated water to dissipate, and then put it in the soil.",
